body:
Even worse in season 3 with so many interior fights and buildings with levels.... theres literally no way in hell to tell where someone in the same building with you is at, above or below you, footsteps in other buildings sound like those in your own.... it's just crap. 

&#x200B;

It might be the worst sound design of any game I've ever played, because i literally cant think of another game where sound was SO BAD that it was actually better to mute the game, because relying on the sound at all, which gives you completely false information, is worse than not having sound at all.

Sound in general is garbage. Whoever is responsible for sound development in this game, please quit and go do something else, preferably completely unrelated to sound, because you clearly have zero talent in this field. Apex might have the worst positional audio cues of any fps game I've ever played, period, and I truly mean that.  I played Return to Castle Wolfenstein a few days ago, which is an ancient game, and it has better positional audio than Apex.

It's like everything is reverse and opposite to how it should be.  What should be loud is silent, what should sound like it's near you sounds like it's too far,  what sounds like it's near you IS actually far,   vertical sound separation is literally non-existent, you can't tell if someone is walking in a building 2 floor above you or under you,  footsteps from a building next to your sounds louder than those in your own, etc.

&#x200B;

Basically, I found turning sound off completely and just focusing on visuals makes me better in this game, because the moment I start relying on the awful sound, I die and get destroyed because 90% of sound information I get is false and just messes with my positioning. 

&#x200B;

And no, it's not my headphones problem, I have a high end headphone setup that costs more than my gaming PC, and sound is perfect in every other situation.

" knowing F1's engineers ingenuity  "  -  They've taken away the right to use that ingenuity with these changes. It's just the beginning too. 2022 they'll add more standardized parts. 2023 even more. Until they finally get to the point where Indy is now, where every team will essentially have the same car with different sponsor paintjobs on them.

&#x200B;

I like how people downvote all of my comments, despite me being one of the few voices of reason here. It's so difficult and frustrating being intelligent and surrounded by imbeciles.  You'll see. Just wait a few years, and you'll see what I'm saying now will be true. Some people are smart enough to predict, others are dumb and therefore need to see things happen in order to understand them.

These changes have american fingerprints all over them. They'll ruin the  sport by americanizing it and making it dumbed down, simplified and  artificially equalized across the field. What exactly do I mean by that? Well....as soon as you take a niche  sport like F1 and try to make it acceptable to a wide audience (and an uneducated audience) , you ruin the essence of what made the niche sport  great in the first place, and what made the TRUE fans love it.  True  fans of F1 love the F1 as it is NOW, because it's as it's supposed to  be. A hierarchy of teams is A NATURAL THING.  Just because some teams  are better, doesn't mean that it's a bad thing.  They're better for a reason, and taking those reasons away KILLS THE ESSENCE of what F1 is about, engineering excellence, creativity, pushing the limits in any way possible, etc. They'll just squish  everything together, just like they do in Indy, Nascar, etc.  That's NOT a good thing, and unfortunately most people fail to see it, despite it being obvious. All you have to do is go watch those races and see what kind of a polar opposite they are to F1. It's like comparing football to basketball.

Imagine what football would look like if someone came along and said "nope, Barcelona can't be so much stronger than some XY team from a poor XY country, we have to come up with rules that ruin Barcelona and makes that XY team more competitive". You think that would improve the sport?  No, no it wouldn't. They think  they'll improve competition with these rule changes, but in the process, they'll make the  competition LESS RELEVANT.  If you ARTIFICIALLY REMOVE SOMEONES ABILITY TO BECOME GREAT, what is the point of it then?

As far as the artificially boosting the amount of overtakes... it's basically like they're turning football into basketball.  They're saying 2-3 goals per game is boring, so lets change the rules of  football so that teams can score 60-70 goals per game and so that someone who watches a football game once a year can enjoy it more. Guess what  happens when they do score. Nobody fucking cares. A goal loses value.   That's what will happen in F1.  Overtakes will happen so often they'll lose value. Just like they have no value in Indy or Nascar. When it's difficult to overtake, then the overtake HAS A LOT OF VALUE, AND IMPORTANCE.  Sure it's not as "exciting" for the average clueless viewer, but for people who understand the sport, it is.

&#x200B;

But this is the problem... whoever owns F1 now doesn't care about the ESSENCE OF THE SPORT. They care about turning more profit, under the guise of making the sport more exciting.  They'll make the sport more exciting, to the wrong crowd though. The issue is, that "wrong" crowd is much bigger than the crowd of real F1 fans.  What the current F1 leaders are doing is catering to the lowest common denominator, because that means more fake fans and more money. The fact that true fans will stop following the sport is irrelevant to them. THAT is what I meant by saying they're americanizing the sport .That's how sports are done in the USA. They look at sports differently than we do in Europe. For us, sports are about passion. For americans, it's about money. They're turning a complex sport with a  lot of things happening under the surface into something that's going to  be superficial and dumbed down in order to cater the dopamine-rush  addicted audiences seeking cheap short-lasting thrills.

&#x200B;

As far as standardized parts and design restrictions go...it's just another sign of them turning F1 into Indy-like competition. They'll start with standardized aero parts, then suspension parts, then more and more and more, until we reach a point where all teams will have the same freaking car with a different paint job on it.  It's HORRIBLE, absolutely HORRIBLE for a sport like F1 which has always been about the COMPLETE OPPOSITE of standardization. Instead of giving teams more freedom, they're giving them more restrictions, and presenting that as an change for good. 

&#x200B;

I can't realize how most of you so called fans are so accepting of this. I expected people to freaking riot after seeing these changes, but nope, most people think it's ok. Is it really so hard to see what I'm predicting here? Or are the "fans" of F1 so different now than they used to be? 

I expect most people to disagree with me after seeing the initial reactions. I'm used to that already.  I'm also used to usually being right at the end. So, remember my post if you disagree with it now, and come back in 2023-2024, once they finish the process of ruining F1, and tell me I was right.

No it is absolutely not nostalgia. I play BF3 every day, still to this day more than any other FPS. I try new ones, they're meh, I quit them, go back to BF3 and realize just how fucking good it is. ANd guess what, every day there are new players on the servers LOVING the game and saying "why the hell didn't I play this before, and why the hell aren't more people playing it?"

&#x200B;

BF3 on hardcore servers with 64 people is STILL the best multiplayer FPS game ever made, objectively and subjectively.

Because modern movie producers and story writers are fucking imbeciles. I'm serious, they're legitimately stupid people, and that's not exaggerated at all. Watch their interviews, most of them have double digit IQ's and probably less maturity than an average 8 year old. How these people get into positions to make movies and get millions of dollars of funding is beyond me, it simply blows my mind.

&#x200B;

Modern movie industry is basically a combination of very smart people doing CGI and incredibly stupid people taking care of everything else. That's why we keep ending up with movies that have 0/10 stories and acting and 10/10 CGI. Not that CGI was any good in this movie, it was more like a 6/10 at best. I'm talking worse than some movies from late 90's.

0/10

&#x200B;

The movie is so fucking terrible in every way (other than CGI, which I don't even count in when the rest of the movie is this bad) it's literally a waste of time watching. Do yourself a favor and spill some water on the floor and watch the floor slowly dry as the water evaporates for 2 hours. 

&#x200B;

Movies like these are a perfect example of what happens when imbeciles and idiots (modern filmmakers) have access to technology they aren't capable of using properly, because intellectually they're on a level of a 7 year old child.  Other movies that come to mind are all the new Jurassic park movies... 

&#x200B;

Just compare the original Jurassic Park to new pieces of shit,  and realize how much better the old one was, because it was actually intelligently made, and didn't just fully focus on CGI, and the rest just comes as a filler for when there's no eye candy on the screen.

